4098.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T20:12:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135214130,imgsize-34632.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why do people overpay for used cars with mileage just below round numbers?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135209780.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent study showed that used car dealers profit from mileage readings just under round-number thresholds. The researchers analyzed millions of transactions to determine pricing impacts of left-digit bias. Buyers often overlook minor differences in mileage, focusing instead on the first digit. This inattention allows dealers to charge more for cars that appear to be better value.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-do-people-overpay-for-used-cars-with-mileage-just-below-round-numbers-researchers-examining-texas-car-transactions-found-that-dealers-earned-46-to-168-extra-at-certain-mileage-thresholds/articleshow/135209780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-do-people-overpay-for-used-cars-with-mileage-just-below-round-numbers-researchers-examining-texas-car-transactions-found-that-dealers-earned-46-to-168-extra-at-certain-mileage-thresholds/articleshow/135209780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T20:06:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135210062,imgsize-1032802.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California artists made an 82-foot whale from 5,000 pounds of plastic, earning national recognition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135213123.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ethyl the Whale, an impressive 82-foot sculpture, currently resides at Santa Fe Community College in New Mexico. Designed by artists Joel Dean Stockdill and Yustina Salnikova, this monumental piece is crafted from approximately 5,000 pounds of discarded plastic. It draws attention to the crisis of ocean pollution and showcases how art can be born from trash, serving as a vital monument for sustainability and environmental awareness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-california-artists-turned-around-5000-pounds-of-discarded-plastic-into-an-82-foot-blue-whale-in-2018-after-moving-to-new-mexico-the-record-setting-sculpture-was-named-a-roadside-america-sight-of-the-week-in-2026/articleshow/135213123.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-california-artists-turned-around-5000-pounds-of-discarded-plastic-into-an-82-foot-blue-whale-in-2018-after-moving-to-new-mexico-the-record-setting-sculpture-was-named-a-roadside-america-sight-of-the-week-in-2026/articleshow/135213123.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T19:34:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135213642,imgsize-813822.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Missouri teen killed on highway; suspect linked to another shooting days earlier]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135211880.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-17-year-old-missouri-girl-was-killed-while-driving-to-a-halloween-party-days-later-prosecutors-linked-the-suspect-to-another-highway-shooting-and-said-a-rifle-and-ammunition-were-recovered-from-his-hotel-room/articleshow/135211880.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://tim